rexit ears at one event of my  constituency we established there were  seven different views of doing brexit  through our brexit ears but the key  thing is a Conservative Party cannot be  a one nation party can only talk to half  the population I mean you've had some  issues haven't used one with your local  Association you've faced three attempt  to do selections and a vote of  no-confidence I mean are people trying  to get rid of you well that's the space  of and nine years over there is a to  refer to my association there is a small  cabal that always see every election  cycle as a reason to have another go and  and get get rid of me and I've got quite  used to what I knew who they are and you  know some of what I just Phillips the  same has echoes with me undermine things  you do twist everything because that is  their objective so why is that better  why are they trying to who knows I mean  I am the my speculation is that for  saintly from here from what song am I  saying I'm in many ways I'm probably a  step in modernization too far for them  you know I think some of them this  particular group of people have Tory  heads and you  hearts but I made it I made a judgment  call at the start of the when I in this  practice process I spent several years  implementing pressure as a minister but  then ultimately when I saw Tomatoes  amazed brexit deal I said this comes to  the question of what am I in politics  for and we've got to have the guts to  say to people the truth that we see  we're now at a point where we're willing  to go ahead and do things that we know  in some cases are not right because we  can't face telling people that there are  contradictions that doesn't mean we  don't do it but it means people should  be fully aware of all the difficulties  and complexities of delivering brexit  I'll give you one example that I have  challenged with this group of people the  idea of an extension to article 50 and I  say Greenland small Greenland 50  population fif